          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "stem": "A miniature microchip sensor has a width of \\\\(3\\\\text{ cm}\\) and \\\\(2\\\\text{ mm}\\\\). Express this width in centimetres as a decimal.",
          "options": [
            "\\\\(3.2\\\\text{ cm}\\\\)",
            "\\\\(3.5\\\\text{ cm}\\\\)",
            "\\\\(3.22\\\\text{ cm}\\\\)",
            "\\\\(3.02\\\\text{ cm}\\\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "hint": "Recall that \\\\(10\\\\text{ mm} = 1\\\\text{ cm}\\\\). Convert the millimetres to centimetres first, then add it to the whole centimetre value.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Identify the measurement components and the conversion factor. The width is \\\\(3\\\\text{ cm}\\) and \\\\(2\\\\text{ mm}\\\\), and we know that \\\\(10\\\\text{ mm} = 1\\\\text{ cm}\\\\).",
              "work": "\\\\(\\text{Conversion Factor: } 10\\\\text{ mm} = 1\\\\text{ cm}\\\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Convert the \\\\(2\\\\text{ mm}\\) component into centimetres by dividing by \\\\(10\\\\). This shifts the digit one place value down.",
              "work": "\\\\(2\\\\text{ mm} = \\\\frac{2}{10}\\\\text{ cm} = 0.2\\\\text{ cm}\\\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Add the converted centimetre decimal to the original \\\\(3\\\\text{ cm}\\) to get the final total length.",
              "work": "\\\\(3\\\\text{ cm} + 0.2\\\\text{ cm} = 3.2\\\\text{ cm}\\\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Conclude that the decimal equivalent of the width is 3.2 cm.",
              "work": "\\\\(\\text{Total Width} = 3.2\\\\text{ cm}\\\\)"
            }
          ],
          "xp": 2
        },
        {
